  "id": "COMPOUND:42173 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Quadrangularic Acid L and Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions. Quadrangularic Acid L is implicated in targeting Thymic stromal lymphopoietin, which is a known target of Cholesteryl arachidonate and 3alpha-Hydroxyolean-11-en-28,13beta-olide. These compounds, in turn, are linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a possible pathway where Quadrangularic Acid L may influence the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C through the activation of Thymic stromal lymphopoietin. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.6074) suggest a strong, reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Quadrangularic Acid L and Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
